{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/995603-need-more-languages","id":995603,"title":"Need more Languages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-30T06:29:29-07:00","id":995603,"title":"Need more Languages","content":"I am about to be in a M20 game and am planning on playing a member of House Shaea, which traditionally know 7+ languages and learn more as they progress. In older editions this was not too difficult as you could just buy a few dots in Linguistics. (I believe there was a merit somewhere that increased the amount as well, though I don't remember what or where)<br /> <br /> In M20 though, starting with 7 languages in a huge investment. To play a hyperpolyglot is impossible. I find this to be at odds to the system because you can play a prodigy in any field by just starting at 5 dots in the appropriate ability (4 BP total vs all of your BP for Languages).<br /> <br /> Has anyone else come up with a house rule better than using the Linguistics skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:01:30-07:00","id":995612,"title":"","content":"V20 introduced the Natural Linguist (2 pt) Merit, which had the duel benefit of giving the character three extra dice on verbal or written language rolls, and making every purchase of the Language merit count double (1 point buys two languages instead of one). So for seven freebie points, you can buy 10 languages instead of just seven. More, if you take Flaws.<br /> <br /> Not sure why M20 didn't include that merit. Actually I do know why: space. The M20 core book was crammed enough as it was. Still seems weird, on account of Mages often having more than enough justification for knowing a whole bunch of tongues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:00:38-07:00","id":996149,"title":"","content":"Dont forget that if you possess 5 or more language merits you can decipher other languages you dont know M20 pg 643 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you possess five Language Merits or more, then you\u2019ve begun to understand the principles of language itself and can try to unravel languages you don\u2019t already know (Intelligence + Enigmas, difficulty 7 or higher). </div> </div> </div>As for what that means I would use the following successes chart (adapted from the rules for Spirit Manipulation: Astral Cant in Guild to the Camarilla pg 106)<ul><li>1 success: Pigdin language; very simple words and phrases can be comprehended.</li> <li>2 successes: Simple sentences are possible; &quot;trade language.&quot;</li> <li>3 successes: Fluent conversation; sufficient for most conversations.</li> <li>4 successes: Complex issues such as meta-physics can be discussed.</li> <li>5 successes: Even the most obscure idiomatic expressions and forms of humor come through.</li> </ul><br /> If you wanted to make it more powerful you could say that with 6+ successes or perhaps having to decipher the same language some number of times; the Mage deciphers the language to the point that they now can take the language merit for that language for free.<br /> <br /> Another house rule you might add is if two people both try to communicate with each other using this rule they can add their successes together for the purpose of both their understanding as they realize what the other is trying to do and begin to work together to figure out the basics and structures of what they are saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:13:31-07:00","id":996195,"title":"","content":"I would mix the old linguistic ability with the new merit. The more languages you know, the easier it is to gather more.<br /> My solution: each rank of the language merit gives additional languages equal to the number of languages you already are capable with. So 1 for the first rank, 2 for the second, then 4, then 8, then 16 at last.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:38:17-07:00","id":996383,"title":"","content":"I personally never found, as an ST, a good rule for Language. I try something new each time I play, and I can say that the developers have the same problem in WoD. Ability or Merit, Language almost never worked the same way twice.<br /> <br /> Sincerely, the only system I personally know that worked it well enough was Mutants &amp; Masterminds 2nd Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T23:56:44-07:00","id":996472,"title":"","content":"A relatively simple house rule I've used just because paying or languages that are rarely meaningful in play rather than for characterization:<br /> <br /> For every one following Abilities (if in use for Secondaries), the character can select one language at 2, 4, and 5 dots. These languages are academic, ritual, liturgical, or similar in nature, that the character cannot communicate or translate fluently. Small and/or common phrases will be easily translated, but anything more requires a roll to accomplish:<br /> <br /> Academics, Esoterica (if languages are important to the practice), Occult, Religion, Culture, Streetwise/Area Knowledge (if the location has a large number of ethnic communities).<br /> <br /> If a player decides to purchase the language as a full language they can pick a new free language that is appropriate at a reasonable time.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> This makes sure purchased languages are reserved for ones that will actually matter to regular play, while a Hermetic can work in Latin, ancient Greek, and Enochian for ritual purposes using appropriate Abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:54:32-07:00","id":996490,"title":"","content":"Or the Storyteller could just Golden Rule it, and let your character have as many languages as seems believable. If a character's familiarity with Sumerian only comes up once in fifty game sessions, it might be easier to just handwave it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T01:27:34-07:00","id":996494,"title":"","content":"I've found that approach can do more harm than good with Mage.<br /> <br /> A lot of mages use language in one form or another as an important element of magic itself. Your character might not have a reason outside of magic to have Sumerian come up more than once every fifty sessions, but for magic it could come up all the time.<br /> <br /> For anything that's a major instrument for a lot of mages, there should be some level of mechanical guidance around it, or it runs into issues. If nothing else it makes sure the ST and players are on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:36:09-07:00","id":996649,"title":"","content":"On the other hand the amount of skill in Sumerian (latin, greek, sanskrit) needed is more or less equal to the amount needed by a choir performing a chant in latin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:41:43-07:00","id":996817,"title":"","content":"Yeah. That's why I ended up with a house rule that meant most mages would have a handful of academic/ritual languages. A character that has a language as an important part of their instruments only needs 2 dots in one of a handful of Abilities (and most of them are ones that most mages have far more investment in) to cover being familiar enough to read and chant something without necessarily knowing the exact meaning without sitting down in a library to translate it fully.<br /> <br /> It doesn't hurt that one of my regular players is, like the OP's original issue, a huge fan of the Shaea and appreciated being able to have most of the requirements covered by investing in standard Abilities, so Language Merit purchases could be saved for ones that mattered more for play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:38:09-07:00","id":996923,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the input, I will take these ideas to my ST and see what we can come up with. I appreciate all the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}